{
  "version": 1,
  "unreferencedRole": "archive",
  "bucket": "miguelemosreverte/mr-pinpin-archive",
  "roots": [
    "docs"
  ],
  "extensions": [
    ".png",
    ".webp",
    ".jpg",
    ".jpeg",
    ".gif",
    ".svg",
    ".ico",
    ".glb",
    ".gltf",
    ".mp4",
    ".webm",
    ".mov",
    ".bin",
    ".gz",
    ".pdf",
    ".woff",
    ".woff2",
    ".ttf",
    ".otf",
    ".blend",
    ".wav",
    ".mp3",
    ".ogg"
  ],
  "managedSymlinks": [
    "docs/storyboard/models/pinpin-v3/model.glb",
    "docs/storyboard/models/pinpin-v3/renders"
  ],
  "manifestSeeds": [
    {
      "path": "docs/storyboard/book.json"
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/storyboard/illustrations.json"
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/storyboard/covers.json"
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/storyboard/family-sprites.json"
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/storyboard/family-production.json"
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/storyboard/family-faces.json"
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/storyboard/family-production-blinks.json"
    },
    {
      "path": "docs/storyboard/atlas-video.json",
      "select": [
        "variants"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "manifestDirectories": [
    "docs/storyboard/stories"
  ],
  "resolutionBases": [
    "docs/storyboard",
    "docs"
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Production allowlist preserves the audited reader, original book, both chapter editions, all four cover registries regardless of approval, standalone stories, atlas modes and fallbacks, and vendored dependencies.",
    "On catalog refresh, supported binary assets under docs default to archive unless explicitly allowlisted or referenced by the configured production manifests. Code and provenance stay in Git.",
    "New manifest asset references automatically extend production. Direct HTML/CSS/JS paths require an explicit production entry; computed paths and fallbacks retain the audited allowlist. New extensions, roots or registries require policy updates. Build checks reject dangling local references but cannot infer arbitrary computed URLs.",
    "Archive includes review, comparison, model, video experiments and historical artwork. The public HF bucket stores their bytes; local review pages use assets:pull to restore their original paths and are not part of the Pages artifact.",
    "archive.gitignore is a proposal only. Apply exclusions only after verified HF receipts. Re-run after merging remote story/cover changes."
  ],
